"{\"content\":\"Specification: abs — Absolute Value of an Integer\\n\\n1. Overview\\n    abs is a total function on the integers Z, mapping each integer to a\\n    non-negative integer.\\n\\n2. Signature\\n    abs : Z -> Z\\n\\n3. Definition\\n    For all x in Z:\\n\\n        abs(x) =  x   if x >= 0\\n        abs(x) = -x   if x <  0\\n\\n4. Expected Properties\\n    For all integers x:\\n\\n        P1 (Non-negativity):  abs(x) >= 0\\n        P2 (Identity case):   abs(x) =  x    if x >= 0\\n        P3 (Negation case):   abs(x) = -x    if x <  0\\n\\n5. Notes\\n    - P1 follows from P2 and P3, since both branches return a\\n      non-negative value for every x in Z.\\n    - abs is idempotent: abs(abs(x)) = abs(x) for all x in Z.\\n    - abs(x) = 0 if and only if x = 0.\\n\",\"path\":\"spec.txt\"}"